     "text": "```json\n{\"reachable\": false, \"rationale\": \"Every exfiltration technique (exfiltrate_db, exfiltrate_fileserver, exfiltrate_backup) needs admin on db, fileserver or backup. Each of those needs a foothold from an auth_* technique that requires stolen_dbadmin. stolen_dbadmin comes only from dump_dbadmin_dc (needs admin_dc) or dump_dbadmin_adfs (needs admin_adfs). Those need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, which come only from auth_dc and auth_adfs. Both require NOT mfa_admin, and the deployed mfa:admin defence blocks them. The attacker can still get a foothold (for example via exploit_web or phishing), reach the internal network, reach appserver and apiserver, and steal admin credentials through kerberoasting. However, there is no other path to foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, so stolen_dbadmin is never obtained and exfiltrated cannot become true.\"}\n```"
    }
